🟠 **High** `agent-awareness/remoteRegistration.ts:1147`

A sign-out during `loadPreferences()` still lets this continuation prime a Live Activity with the pre-sign-out snapshot, recreating a card containing the signed-out account’s thread data after cleanup. `refreshWidget` checks the provider identity before the preference read, so recheck `relayTokenProvider` and `relayTokenProviderIdentity` afterward and return before priming.

```diff
     }).pipe(Effect.orElseSucceed(() => null));
+    if (!relayTokenProvider || relayTokenProviderIdentity !== identity) {
+      return;
+    }
```

🟠 **High** `agent-awareness/remoteRegistration.ts:1081`

An obsolete refresh for account A can supersede account B’s in-flight snapshot and leave B’s widget stuck on Loading. When A’s token registration completes, `refreshWidget` increments the shared `widgetSnapshotReads` before checking `identity`, so B’s result is discarded even though A’s result is rejected. Check the captured account identity before incrementing the counter or starting the read.

```suggestion
  const refreshWidget = Effect.gen(function* () {
    if (!relayTokenProvider || relayTokenProviderIdentity !== identity) {
      return undefined;
    }
    const read = ++widgetSnapshotReads;
    const snapshot = yield* readAgentActivitySnapshot();
```
